{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792945819,"nonce":"TCWHhUxVnalStMpoCjkOke9SraI=","title":"Session on Cloudflare: a Durable Object runner and a GitHub sign-in Worker","message":"native/session's core (store, programs and authority traits, no tokio) needs a second runner: a Durable Object that keeps the workspace in its own storage (SQLite or R2), hibernating WebSockets, alarms for the flush delay, a clock from the Worker. Plus the edge: a Worker that runs GitHub OAuth (or Cloudflare Access with GitHub as the identity provider) and signs the {login, id, exp} credential with the secret it shares with the object, as docs/session.md describes. A Durable Object runs no processes: anything that spawns haxe or caribou needs a Cloudflare Container behind it (tracked separately).\n\nPart of the browser epic: git-bug ae3a156433377383faa317d5da1f34e6eab10f9a6e0d0ab0456fc0e0277a8382","files":null}]}